     Why a repalette and not a different rotation. Item 8's rule is that each of the
     thirty-three wears its donor's palette rotated. For these six no rotation works:
     none of their donors has a 4550 slot in its own "modelRecolorFind", so the face
     colour has nowhere in the array to stay and every rotation moves it onto
     something that is not a face. That is proved rather than asserted, in
     AuthoredRecordsTest.noRotationOfThoseSixDonorsCouldHaveHeldTheFaceColourInPlace.

     No upstream record was repaletted, and that is not deference. Twelve shipped
     records paint 4550 onto a slot aimed at something else; the six that are not
     ours are "Forester", "Nicholson", "Assistant Apothecary", "Mary" and "Silver
     merchant", which paint an arm or a hand — models 176, 353, 159 and 27139 are a
